{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/3843-exalted-2-5-solars-unbalanced","id":3843,"title":"exalted 2.5 solars unbalanced","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-05T16:27:54-08:00","id":3843,"title":"exalted 2.5 solars unbalanced","content":"Counting the charms and advantages of solasr ,\u00bfNot seem to be well above the other exalteds,?(abysals,infernals ,lunars)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/429-magius","name":"magius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar429_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T16:43:09-08:00","id":3852,"title":"","content":"Solars more powerful then the other Exalted? Working as intended.<br /> <br /> They're making the gap a bit smaller in 3e though, or so I hear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/673-requiem_jeer","name":"Requiem_Jeer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar673_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T16:47:41-08:00","id":3857,"title":"","content":"Not exactly sure of what you're getting at here, but the 2.5 errata was mostly focused on Solars because they're the number one splat and some of the other splats had massive issues that needed an edition change so Solars got more attention as a result. 2.5 was only supposed to be a band-aid anyway, no one expected it to 'fix' the game's fundamental problems it was just intended to make playing a Solar out of the core book less of a headache.<br /> <br /> edit: notice that the 2.5 errata dealt almost entirely with core book material. Because the other splats don't have charms in the core book their charms weren't changed very much, if at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":407,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/407-ithle","user":"Ithle","date":". 11-05-2013, 11:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/407-ithle","name":"Ithle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T16:49:46-08:00","id":3861,"title":"","content":"For example melee solar or martial arts solars ,some are more powerful than infernal or abysal charms of combat","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/429-magius","name":"magius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar429_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T17:43:04-08:00","id":3888,"title":"","content":"Funny you mention Martial Arts. There are these people known as sidereals who'd like to have a word with you. No. Forgetting them is a common occurance I hear...<br /> <br /> Really though. This is like saying the sky is blue, or the sun in Malfeas is green radiation fabulous. Its not a secret that Solars in 2.5 can easily become balance breakers. Thing is, raw power doesn't always win the day. Infernals and Abyssals get something that solars distinctly lack. Like say mentors, infrastructure, support, ready access to nice things (So long as overlords remain pleased), etc.<br /> <br /> Each splat has it's own path to broken, you just have to look around until you see how the pieces fit together.<br /> <br /> Edit: Since Abyssals and Infernals are technically solaroids, I figure I should throw in something for lunars and dragonbloods too. Lunars can literally cheese a few charms/knacks that literally let them catch up to anything regardless of it's speed. Like say the five metal shrike or blazing solar chariot. Which boggles the mind when you consider it would mean crossing insane distances in short periods of time because you <i>really</i> want to eat that Frisbee. Then you have your DBs whose war charms make them more powerful the more there are. Its inverse conservation of ninjutsu, (Combined with solar war charms leading them...well primordial feel for good reasons....) at it's finest. Siddies, well they are MIB Fate/Time ninjas who hide in teacups and punch you into duck. And best martial artists. Solars can barely learn their smooth moves....with lots of effort and one of them teaching. Chances of that are pretty slim without PC/Party interaction though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":731,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/731-lurker","user":"Lurker","date":". 11-05-2013, 08:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/731-lurker","name":"Lurker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar731_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T03:41:56-08:00","id":4187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lurker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/3843-exalted-2-5-solars-unbalanced?p=3888#post3888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Funny you mention Martial Arts. There are these people known as sidereals who'd like to have a word with you. No. Forgetting them is a common occurance I hear...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I do not mencion siderals ,they have the best styles of martial arts ,but if a solar can learn these styles and infernal and abysal no .....<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/429-magius","name":"magius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar429_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T04:11:14-08:00","id":4199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>magius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/3843-exalted-2-5-solars-unbalanced?p=4187#post4187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not mencion siderals ,they have the best styles of martial arts ,but if a solar can learn these styles and infernal and abysal no .....</div> </div> </div> </div>Solars can theoretically learn SMA, sure, but it's a bit... silly for them, in 2e. 12 xp a charm, and they pay more to use them than Sidereals because they lack sutras. The only reason it's ever worthwhile for a Solar to learn SMA in 2e is because some of the styles are flatly broken.<br /> <br /> (There is a huge laundry list of attendant problems and related issues and various arguments inherent in the above paragraph, but that's just a quick summary of how it is. A bigger problem, for the topic at hand, is that the generally mechanically-broken nature of most SMA limits its usefulness to <i>Sidereals</i> in a typical game, as do its outrageously high Essence minimums.)<br /> <br /> 2.5e is a quick patch to a broken system focused mainly on making Solars playable, though -- they didn't want to spend more time on that because they ultimately felt the game needed an entirely new system to fix its underlying issues; a fix for every problem in 2e would basically read something like &quot;replace all text in every book with the following:&quot;<br /> <br /> Lunars and Sidereals have underlying issues that would've basically required a total rewrite of their splatbook to fix. Infernals have issues that make them nearly impossible to adapt to 2.5e without writing insane amounts of material. (You can still play them, but they're currently somewhat limited in the builds available to them -- absent extensive homebrew, Malfeas is not optional if you want to be really good at combat, because they have no other way to get decent magical soak.)<br /> <br /> Alchemicals are usable, I think, but remember that they're intended to be the weakest Celestials. Honestly, 2.5e probably indirectly buffed them a bit, since their big weakness was their terribly overpriced perfect defenses, and those are now no longer as central to combat.<br /> <br /> But yeah, 2.5e is not well-balanced. The best bet is to just wait for 3e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T04:35:10-08:00","id":4209,"title":"","content":"The Solars benefited late on with a certain amount of Charm bloat. They are, after all, the most popular splat in terms of sales (helps that they're in the Core book!) and they were the focus of things like Dreams of the First Age and Glories of the Most High: Unconquered Sun. The net result is that they have way more Charms at way higher levels than just about anyone else, including their &quot;equals,&quot; the Abyssals and Infernals.<br /> <br /> That said, the remedy to this is simply to invent new Charms for the splats. Sadly, not something that's gonna happen in 2.5, but we can help with home-brewing the Charms.<br /> <br /> Now, as for Martial Arts... no, Sidereals can't make you forget them. That was a joke. And technically Sidereals have the best Martial Arts, and technically Solars can learn them, but... have you ever heard the term &quot;opportunity costs?&quot; You spend XP on one thing, you don't get to spend it on another. So you can't just pick up Sidereal Martial Arts at a whim- you need to make a pretty significant investment of experience and time before you can learn even up to the Form Charms, much less the entire Style. And once you put all that together, Sidereals still have Sutras to make wielding SMAs more practical than it would be for Solars or Abyssals.<br /> <br /> Infernals can't learn Sidereal Martial Arts. Long story there, but basically, if you want high-level form Charms as an Infernal, take a shintai. That's what they're there for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;We do not quit playing because we grow old, we grow old because we quit playing.&quot; - Oliver Wendell Holmes","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/283-mrinsecure","name":"MrInsecure","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T07:35:57-08:00","id":4305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/3843-exalted-2-5-solars-unbalanced?p=4199#post4199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But yeah, 2.5e is not well-balanced. The best bet is to just wait for 3e.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would certainly hope 3e is not balanced either. The Solars are meant to be the most powerful. That was one of the core tenets of the setting.<br /> (Though, I guess you could argue Abyssals and Infernals should be equivalent.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/453-megazarak","name":"MegaZarak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T08:06:13-08:00","id":4320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MegaZarak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/3843-exalted-2-5-solars-unbalanced?p=4305#post4305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would certainly hope 3e is not balanced either. The Solars are meant to be the most powerful. That was one of the core tenets of the setting.<br /> (Though, I guess you could argue Abyssals and Infernals should be equivalent.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you are confusing intentional power difference with unbalanced. They are very different beasts. Solars and their peers Abyssals and Infernals standing a head above the rest is rather different from Solars just effortlessly dominating every field forever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25-moonwolf","name":"MoonWolf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T08:06:49-08:00","id":4322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MegaZarak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/3843-exalted-2-5-solars-unbalanced?p=4305#post4305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would certainly hope 3e is not balanced either. The Solars are meant to be the most powerful. That was one of the core tenets of the setting.<br /> (Though, I guess you could argue Abyssals and Infernals should be equivalent.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Balance and equality aren't the same thing. It's not a problem that Solars are the strongest - it is a problem that they can practically godmode through any challenge. The idea is to remove the latter without touching the former.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T08:21:02-08:00","id":4337,"title":"","content":"+1 to Moonwolf and Morangias (I just realized it wasn't spelled Morganias). Solar Exalted should have an edge, but it is not good design if a Solar can respond to any obstacle with a shrug unless it's another Solar. Through large chunks of Second Edition, you were in charge or succeeding only if,<br /> <br /> a.) You were a Solar Exalt<br /> b.) A Solar Exalt wanted it that way.<br /> c.) No Solar Exalt cared enough to interfere.<br /> <br /> Going forward, it looks like a Solar is likely to be bluntly stronger than you in an area of mutual specialty, but depending on how you play your cards victory is not impossible--and you may have some powerful tricks up your sleeve that they can't necessarily duplicate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T14:35:29-08:00","id":4599,"title":"","content":"I came to this thread expecting to say &quot;unbalanced compared to what&quot;, but the 3 M's above me seem to have covered that.<br /> <br /> The Solar Exalted are <i>meant</i> to be more powerful than everyone else.<br /> The Solar Exalted are <i>meant</i> to &quot;break the setting&quot; (that was the reason they were created in the first place).<br /> They are meant to be able to change the world and defeat any opponent you can throw at them.<br /> They are <i>even</i> meant to be better (on the whole) than the Abyssals (who are Solar power turned to a niche use) and Infernals (who are Solar power corrupted).<br /> <br /> That said:<br /> <br /> They are not meant to be better than other Exalts &quot;in their niche&quot; (they're not meant to be better than Abyssal's at necromancy for example - which is not to say that a Solar can't be good at necromancy or an Abyssal can't be bad at it).<br /> They are not meant to be so much better than everyone else that nothing is a challenge.<br /> They are not meant to be better due to twinky min-maxing the character generation mini-game.<br /> They are meant to break the <i>world</i>, not break the <i>story</i>.<br /> They are not meant to make the game unfun for everyone else (which is not to say that people have a right to play non-Solars and expect not to suck compared to the Solars, but it is meant as an indication that one Solar build can easily overshadow the other PCs (whether they are Solars or not) and this quickly leads to people losing interest and feeling frustrated).<br /> <br /> So in answer to your complaint: yes, Solar charms are better than Abyssal Charms and Infernal Charms. They are meant to be. Players are meant to play Solars. You can play any splat you like, but you need to understand these splats are <i>weaker</i> than Solars who are <i>intentionally</i> more powerful than everyone else (because they are the faction you are <i>supposed</i> to play in a game that's <i>supposed</i> to change the world).<br /> <br /> Or to use a D&amp;D analogy, you <i>seem</i> to be complaining that Player Class Levels are more powerful than NPC Classes/Racial Levels: this is an intentional, and fundamental, part of the game. If you are <i>actually</i> complaining that the Wizard Class is more powerful than the Monk Class, then I apologise: you are right and I hope that this is fixed next edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T16:56:42-08:00","id":4726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/3843-exalted-2-5-solars-unbalanced?p=4322#post4322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Balance and equality aren't the same thing. It's not a problem that Solars are the strongest - it is a problem that they can practically godmode through any challenge. The idea is to remove the latter without touching the former.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, but they aren't supposed to be equal or balanced. Unbalanced doesn't mean unbeatable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/453-megazarak","name":"MegaZarak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T17:10:39-08:00","id":4734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MegaZarak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/3843-exalted-2-5-solars-unbalanced?p=4726#post4726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, but they aren't supposed to be equal or balanced. Unbalanced doesn't mean unbeatable.</div> </div> </div> </div>[ATTACH=CONFIG]n68[/ATTACH]<br /> <br /> More seriously, yes, Solars are definitely supposed to be balanced, because balance or lack thereof is a matter of game rules' quality and not of comparative power between character options (it only becomes the latter incidentally when balance - i.e. quality - is absent from the game).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T17:58:48-08:00","id":4752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/3843-exalted-2-5-solars-unbalanced?p=4734#post4734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[ATTACH=CONFIG]n68[/ATTACH]<br /> <br /> More seriously, yes, Solars are definitely supposed to be balanced, because balance or lack thereof is a matter of game rules' quality and not of comparative power between character options (it only becomes the latter incidentally when balance - i.e. quality - is absent from the game).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure you misunderstand what balance means. Balance means thing A is roughly equivalent to thing B. They are in &quot;balance&quot;. Its not related to the quality of the rules at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/453-megazarak","name":"MegaZarak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T18:46:25-08:00","id":4782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/3843-exalted-2-5-solars-unbalanced?p=4734#post4734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[ATTACH=CONFIG]n68[/ATTACH]<br /> <br /> More seriously, yes, Solars are definitely supposed to be balanced, because balance or lack thereof is a matter of game rules' quality and not of comparative power between character options (it only becomes the latter incidentally when balance - i.e. quality - is absent from the game).</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be more accurate to say that Solars are meant to adhere to an inequal balance.<br /> <br /> As a Solar, you are supposed to be able to defeat any other splat in an area of shared specialty. If you are of equal experience and specialization it should not be trivial, and there is a reasonable chance that you might lose even though the odds are weighted in your favor.<br /> <br /> As a non-Solar, a Solar should be something you find yourself having to be wary around, and if they share an area of specialization with you you may have to ask for help where you wouldn't otherwise. It should not be a good idea to kill any newborn Solar you see on sight because the moment they get some XP they'll be able to tell you to get on your knees and make you like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T09:38:52-08:00","id":5151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MegaZarak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/3843-exalted-2-5-solars-unbalanced?p=4752#post4752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure you misunderstand what balance means. Balance means thing A is roughly equivalent to thing B. They are in &quot;balance&quot;. Its not related to the quality of the rules at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not in roleplaying games, it doesn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-08T04:53:10-08:00","id":5815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/3843-exalted-2-5-solars-unbalanced?p=5151#post5151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not in roleplaying games, it doesn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's closer to &quot;A may be better than B at X, but B is better than A at Y&quot;. Or alternately, &quot;A is 20% better than B at any given X of investment, as a stated fact. If A is 50% better than B at it given equal X of investment, then something has become imbalanced&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-08T05:12:26-08:00","id":5823,"title":"","content":"Actually it's more like &quot;people are having fun and things are working as intended&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-08T05:51:57-08:00","id":5840,"title":"","content":"Balance is a holistic thing when it comes to roleplaying games - if it was mathematically achievable, we'd be having perfectly balanced game engines for at least ten years all across the industry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-08T06:01:44-08:00","id":5847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/3843-exalted-2-5-solars-unbalanced?p=5840#post5840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Balance is a holistic thing when it comes to roleplaying games - if it was mathematically achievable, we'd be having perfectly balanced game engines for at least ten years all across the industry.</div> </div> </div> </div>And due to the open natureof the game, it requires the players to not be dicks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-08T14:07:32-08:00","id":6322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Couch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/3843-exalted-2-5-solars-unbalanced?p=4782#post4782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It should not be a good idea to kill any newborn Solar you see on sight because the moment they get some XP they'll be able to tell you to get on your knees and make you like it.</div> </div> </div> </div>As much as I hate that (when I'm not playing a Solar), this fact does make the Wyld Hunt make sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-08T14:33:43-08:00","id":6343,"title":"","content":"Let's not forget something important : not all Solars have all Solar Charms. Because Solars have the potential to be an head ahead everyone else (because one of the elements of their thematics is to be &quot;Prime among pairs&quot;), <i>this doesn't mean that any individual Solar would be better than any given non-Solar character.</i><br /> <br /> If a Solar doesn't invest in defence Charms, even mortal humans can be dangerous to him. If he doesn't get the &quot;I pown opponent class XYZ forever&quot; Charms, then he can't dismiss opponent class XYZ... And even if he does get it, then he might not have enough XP to get the other Creation-shattering Charms. Or to extend his influence to protect all that he cares about while he's busy kung-fu fighting people elsewhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://oi61.tinypic.com/30cn5ug.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> A.K.A. Xelloss33","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/924-xelloss","name":"Xelloss","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar924_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}